# Force LF on the generated structure_key reference-vectors artifact so its bytes are
# platform-stable for every consumer that byte-hashes it. With core.autocrlf=true and
# no .gitattributes, checkout re-materializes CRLF and a raw hash reports a difference
# that isn't one (Unpopped's git-hash-object note). The freshness gate is a BYTE compare,
# so the file must be LF on disk on every platform.
#
# Scoped to this one file deliberately: a corpus-wide *.json renormalization is filed
# separately so its one-time diff does not collide with an open freshness-gate PR.
# Every generated corpus artifact, not just the byte-match reference (#162). The
# freshness gates compare BYTES, and a consumer byte-hashing any of these on a
# CRLF checkout must see what the generator wrote. The one-file scope above was
# deliberate at the time and is now lifted: the renormalization lands in its own
# commit so the one-time diff is reviewable on its own.
conformance/corpus/*.json text eol=lf
